CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*wrk)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct adj_time_work)...)
#72: FILE: drivers/staging/hv/hv_util.c:145:
+	wrk = kmalloc(sizeof(struct adj_time_work), GFP_ATOMIC);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!wrk"
#73: FILE: drivers/staging/hv/hv_util.c:146:
+	if (wrk == NULL)

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

